					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4483018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834604" alt="TheMightyMcB" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4483018)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;" >TheMightyMcB</a></span> <span class="odate time_1537829951 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 Sep 2018 22:59</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4002354">
									

<p>Premise is both nihilistic and fun in just the right amounts. Leaves me with a few questions unanswered<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-584344-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-584344-1')">1</a></sup><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-584344-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-584344-2')">2</a></sup><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-584344-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-584344-3')">3</a></sup><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-584344-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-584344-4')">4</a></sup><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-584344-5" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-584344-5')">5</a></sup><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-584344-6" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-584344-6')">6</a></sup>, so I wouldn't exactly mind if this was elaborated in some way or another, but I still like it as it stands, so take your upvote.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-584344-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-584344-1')">1</a>. Is the TGI Friday's the only space left in the universe after it collapses?</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-584344-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-584344-2')">2</a>. What is the threshold where this starts to happen? Does this only happen after heat-death, XKs, information deletion via black holes, etc?</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-584344-3"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-584344-3')">3</a>. Were the employees created when the first extra-universal TGI Friday's was, or were they just people in the universe who were shoved into the restaurant when it died?</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-584344-4"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-584344-4')">4</a>. Is the law of conservation of mass intact in the remnants of a dead universe, or is everything gone save for what was needed for the TGI Fridays and the food/drinks it makes?</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-584344-5"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-584344-5')">5</a>. Without a reliable and infinite way to measure time, how do the employees handle shifts, eating, and sleeping?</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-584344-6"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-584344-6')">6</a>. I strongly believe that this article would fit nicely into a canon, but I can't decide which one would work best. Part of me really wants this to get added to <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-s-c-plastics-hub">S&amp;C Plastics</a>.</div>
</div>

